        {
          "gid": "1218929162756670",
          "created_at": "2026-09-29T03:35:14.569Z",
          "created_by": {
            "gid": "1217162291350352",
            "name": "Alejandro Milano"
          },
          "text": "",
          "type": "comment",
          "resource_subtype": "comment_added"
        },
        {
          "gid": "1218929162756674",
          "created_at": "2026-09-29T03:35:54.143Z",
          "created_by": {
            "gid": "1217162291350352",
            "name": "Alejandro Milano"
          },
          "text": "fyi - these errors were found by AI. Let's make these correct and check other landing pages that we built recently\n \nThere are avoidable trust inconsistencies. Near the bottom, the page shows “call (303)-421-7611” and then immediately “Prefer to talk? Call (720) 419-3699.” https://www.arvadadentalcenter.com/ads-landing-pages/all-on-x-ads-landing Even if one is a tracking number, the visitor should see one consistent number while dynamic call tracking happens behind the scenes. The FAQ also makes aggressive statements such as “99.9%” same-day teeth and lifetime-oriented claims. https://www.arvadadentalcenter.com/ads-landing-pages/all-on-x-ads-landing I’d use slightly more qualified language on the ad page.\n \nWhat's likely holding the current page back\n    The page is slow. The page code contains two complete copies of the page stacked on top of each other: two heroes, two galleries and two FAQs. It also embeds about eight videos, all loading on page open. On a phone that's slow, and slow pages lose ad clicks.\n    There are three different ways to convert. Visitors get an embedded form, buttons that go to a separate consult page, and a mobile \"Free consult\" button that opens the PatientsReach scheduler. Every extra page or new flow loses people.\n    Your price differs across the site. It's $18,795 on the ad page and cost page, \"starts at $17,795\" on the Dental Implants page, and \"$20,000 to $30,000 per arch\" in the All-on-4 FAQ. Shoppers who compare pages will notice.\n    The phone numbers don't match. One button reads (303) 421-7611 but dials the 720 tracking number. The mobile header on your service pages dials a 719 number, which looks like a leftover bug.\n    The review claim isn't accurate. \"1,300+ Five-Star Reviews\" is off, because Google shows a 4.8 average across about 1,280 reviews. I used \"4.8 on Google, 1,200+ reviews\" instead. Please check the live count.\n    Small typos hurt trust. Examples are \"Book a Appointment,\" \"Clincial,\" and photo text naming a \"Dr. Kim.\"\n",
          "type": "comment",
          "resource_subtype": "comment_added"
        }
      ],
